{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d25bd669-b609-4f45-b74f-f23a044ca23e",
    "name": "📌 SiliconFlow API",
    "description": "### About\n\n\"Lightning-fast AI platform for developers. Deploy, fine-tune, and run 200+ optimized LLMs and multimodal models with simple APIs.\"\n\nSiliconFlow runs open models from other labs, such as DeepSeek, GLM, Kimi, MiniMax and Qwen, through an OpenAI-compatible API, plus embeddings, reranking, image generation and TypeSafe's Kev-4B decision model. On the workspace overview it is listed under **Inference hosts**.\n\n### Prerequisites\n\n- Postman Account\n    \n- SiliconFlow Account: [https://cloud.siliconflow.com/](https://cloud.siliconflow.com/)\n    \n\n### Usage\n\n1. Create a fork\n    \n2. Update collection variables\n    \n3. Send requests\n\nStart with the 🚀 Get Started folder.\n\nAdd your key to your **Postman Vault** as `siliconflow_api_key` (Vault icon in the footer, then **Add secret**, using that exact name). Requests read it as `{{vault:siliconflow_api_key}}`, so your key never leaves your device.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- API: [https://docs.siliconflow.com/en/api-reference/chat-completions/chat-completions](https://docs.siliconflow.com/en/api-reference/chat-completions/chat-completions)\n    \n- Models: [https://cloud.siliconflow.com/models](https://cloud.siliconflow.com/models)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-17T14:22:19.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-10-17T14:22:19.000Z",
    "lastUpdatedBy": "7643177",
    "uid": "7643177-d25bd669-b609-4f45-b74f-f23a044ca23e"
  },
